**This is a route-level bug, and it's serious**, because it means the RMS_ANALYTICS request is falling through to the full RMS creator workflow — which has WRITE access (task creation forms, Excel bulk upload). Analytics is supposed to be strictly READ-ONLY. If a request meant for the analytics collection ends up in the RMS workflow instead, a user could accidentally (or a malicious user deliberately) trigger real data-mutating actions from what should be a read-only analytics interface.

